## Context
GOVERNANCE.md's increment train, item 6 (scoped issue A), per the ratified re-form (DECISIONS.md 2026-08-26).
One #10-shaped issue: documented behaviors, reproductions, measurements, no
code to accept. Carries: the ledger/freshness/counters complex (SPEC.md §5.2.1,
§5.2.4, §5.2.8); the PAUSE defect as motivation (verified: stop cancels one job,
auto_build default-on restarts on the next query — index-tool.ts:56-65,
semantic-search.ts:48-65; the R22 violation); the SERVE-STALE defect as
motivation (verified: dropStaleVectors -> clearVectors() at open,
index-manager.ts:286-308, plus the query-time dimension drop at :889-892 —
semantic coverage zeroed by an upgrade; dropStaleVectors was written on
purpose, so the issue names the alternative reading rather than treating it
as an oversight); the legacy-JSON custody paragraph (R15: a stale
search-index.json retains deleted items' text forever — the folded I-4); and
the D5 query-semantics work riding along or waiting for demand (the verified
repro: "general equilibrium" retrieves either-word today; interim item scope
per SPEC.md §5.2.6). Absorbs the content of closed
tickets 0020, 0021, 0023.

Upstream [#24](https://github.com/oscardvs/zoteus/issues/24), filed by
@StianOby on 2026-08-27, now owns the user-visible resume slice: after a
stopped local-API build, the missing/invalid library version stamp sends the
next run back to zero. Do not open a competing issue. Offer #24 the behavioral
contract this design needs: already committed work survives stop and process
restart; the Zotero version stamp is a freshness signal, not the work cursor;
repeating an interrupted unit is safe; and resumed and uninterrupted builds
converge to the same index. The maintainer remains free to implement that
without this repo's full ledger design.

At v1.8.0 the narrow implementation seam is already visible:
`buildIncremental()` persists partial work (every 200 items or 10 seconds in
the metadata pass; every 500 items or 60 seconds in the full-text pass), and
the reloaded partial index is queryable, but a new full build unconditionally
calls `reset()` and initializes its page cursor at zero.
A small persisted build checkpoint beside the committed rows could carry the
phase and progress identity without overloading `libraryVersion`. The useful
performance bounds are: redo no more than the last uncommitted batch; never
re-embed a committed passage merely because the process restarted; and do not
scan every stored passage merely to find the resume point.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] issue drafted: behaviors + repros + measurements, no code to accept
- [x] #24 comment offers the resume contract; posted 2026-08-28, response pending
- [ ] filed after the PR train resolves (DESIGN §4 ordering)
- [ ] response recorded here; sunset rule applies
